<!-- snippets/jc-buybox-price.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  Hero price block. Sits directly under a hairline divider, above the size
  tiles — the price used to appear seventh in the column, after a badge pill, a
  checklist and a banner promoting a pack the shopper had not selected.

  Reflects the selected size AND plan at once: every figure reads the same
  jc_price getter from jc-buybox-state.liquid, the one the tiles and the CTA
  read, so the hero can never quote a subscription price beside one-time
  per-can rates.

  NO STRIKETHROUGH LIST PRICE. There is no "$71.88" struck out above $65.99
  here, because no such price has ever been charged and a strikethrough asserts
  a former or prevailing one. The saving is stated as a sentence that names its
  comparison instead. The only struck-through figure possible is a real
  compare_at_price set on the variant in Shopify.

  Accepts:
  - block: {object}

  Usage:
    {% render 'jc-buybox-price', block: block %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- capture jc_initial_price %}{% render 'jc-initial-price', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
<div
  class="jc-bb-priceblock w-full"
  x-show="current_variant_exists"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <hr class="jc-bb-rule">

  <div class="jc-bb-price__top">
    <div>
      {%- comment -%}
        The server-rendered figure is the pack the tiles pre-select, not the
        first available variant — see jc-initial-price.liquid. x-text takes over
        on first paint and lands on the same number, so nothing flashes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span
        class="jc-bb-price__main"
        x-text="jcMoney(jc_price)"
      >{{ jc_initial_price | plus: 0 | money }}</span>

      {%- comment -%}
        Real compare_at_price only. x-if rather than x-show so the <s> element
        does not exist in the DOM at all unless the merchant has actually set
        one — no struck-through markup to leak into a screen reader or a
        stylesheet override.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <template x-if="jc_compare_price > 0">
        <s class="jc-bb-price__compare" x-text="jcMoney(jc_compare_price)"></s>
      </template>
    </div>

    <div class="jc-bb-price__unitwrap" x-show="jc_unit_price > 0" x-cloak>
      <span class="jc-bb-price__unit" x-text="jcMoney(jc_unit_price)"></span>
      <span class="jc-bb-price__unit-label">per can</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The saving, as a sentence that names what it is measured against. Same
    baseline the tiles use: the smallest pack on the product, compared under
    whichever plan is currently selected so the two sides are like for like.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p
    class="jc-bb-price__save"
    x-show="!jc_is_base_pack && jc_savings > 0"
    x-cloak
    x-text="`You save ${jcMoney(jc_savings)} versus buying ${jc_base_pack}-can packs`"
  ></p>

  {%- comment -%}
    On the smallest pack there is nothing to save against, so it says so and
    points at the next size up rather than showing an empty slot.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p
    class="jc-bb-price__starter"
    x-show="jc_is_base_pack && jc_next_pack > 0"
    x-cloak
    x-text="`Our starter pack — step up to ${jc_next_pack} cans to start saving`"
  ></p>
</div>
